    fix: floor boundary detection at T_MIN=2 in ad-hoc scripts; regenerate affected reports
    
    run_stakes_sweep.py and compare_prompted_vs_distilled.py each
    reimplemented boundary detection without the T_MIN=2 floor that
    trace_analysis.py's audited hazard_stop_for_group enforces, silently
    reintroducing the exact bug class the 2026-06-20 remediation (commit
    ef45dda) fixed. Both now import the audited function instead of
    reimplementing it; a new structural-guard test
    (research/tests/test_boundary_floor.py) prevents a third recurrence.
    Reports regenerated from real re-runs against existing trace data (no
    GPU needed): Qwen-7B c=0 now correctly reads T*=5 (was 1), DeepSeek
    T*=2 (was 1). Also fixes three prose passages that misdescribed their
    own data tables (stakes-direction claim, DeepSeek repair-rate
    comparison, and July_1_Checkin.md's First Answer row), corrected at
    the generating scripts so the fixes survive re-runs.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016jFunoxRUo9oW212ZjYE14

